      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly!! the \"enhancing\" thing makes so much sense because it feels so manufactured. and when you mention the muscle twitch patterns... that's literally what I'm seeing. it's like the facial structure is right but the way it *moves* is just hollow. i've been reading some threads online where people are saying the real [Celebrity Name] actually went missing or had a breakdown a few years ago and they've been using a high-end digital proxy or a lookalike ever since to keep the brand alive. it would explain why everything feels so polished yet completely soul-less. does that sound like a plausible way for a major studio to handle a crisis like that? like, using a simulated version to maintain continuity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
